# Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Runtime artifacts. All three are machine-specific: a calibration is only valid
# for the exact camera and projector placement that produced it, so it must not
# follow the code to another table. Snapshots are the same in kind -- they are
# frames from one rig's camera and overlays at one projector's resolution, which
# make a debugging session reproducible and are meaningless anywhere else.
#
# The whole snapshots directory rather than a glob: the two tools that write
# there both mkdir it, so nothing breaks on a fresh clone that has never run one.
data/logs/
data/calibration/
data/snapshots/

# Hailo models are large binaries built with the Dataflow Compiler.
models/*.hef
